From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 16:34:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: tas2764: treat a changed register as success on
 the dance path

tas2764_update_pwr_ctrl() returned the shutdown dance helper's result
unchanged. The helper ends with snd_soc_component_update_bits(), which
returns 1 when it changed the register, and both callers in
tas2764_mute() treat any non-zero value as an error:

- unmute: SHUTDOWN -> MUTE returns 1, so tas2764_mute() returns before
  it sets unmuted and writes MUTE -> ACTIVE. The amplifier stays in
  MUTE for the whole stream.
- mute: ACTIVE -> MUTE returns 1, so the ramp wait, stream_stopped and
  the deferred shutdown are skipped. The amplifier is still in MUTE when
  the bus clock stops, and the fault handler reports the clock loss.

Map a positive result to 0, as the plain path already does.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
(cherry picked from commit 784dfcb1beefe5714cd59fdc01147baa49ffe863)
(cherry picked from commit 19d3de6a3318026630096d20c784ea511957adf7)
---
 sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c b/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c
index c7e270376cf..66b16949ec0 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c
@@ -364,8 +364,10 @@ static int tas2764_update_pwr_ctrl(struct tas2764_priv *tas2764)
 	else
 		val = TAS2764_PWR_CTRL_SHUTDOWN;
 
-	if (tas2764_shutdown_dance(tas2764))
-		return tas2764_do_quirky_pwr_ctrl_change(tas2764, val);
+	if (tas2764_shutdown_dance(tas2764)) {
+		ret = tas2764_do_quirky_pwr_ctrl_change(tas2764, val);
+		return ret < 0 ? ret : 0;
+	}
 
 	ret = snd_soc_component_update_bits(component, TAS2764_PWR_CTRL,
 					    TAS2764_PWR_CTRL_MASK, val);
-- 
